 **Numbered Steps:**
 1.  **Positional Encoding:** Encode the input sample position $\mathbf{p}$ using the same positional encoding scheme as FastNeRF [S2, unofficial].
-2.  **Skeletal Deformation:** Compute the bone-deformed position $\mathbf{p}_{bone} = \mathcal{F}_{bone}(\mathbf{p}, \mathbf{e})$. This step accounts for large rigid movements of the head and shoulders [S2, unofficial].
